# The realtime ban list - the static half of FINAL_PLAN §2.2 Rule 1
# (phase_0.md §4.6). Phase 1 adds the dynamic half: an allocator hook that fails
# the test suite if the audio thread allocates.
#
# **Scope is defined by RT_PATHS in tools/lint.py, and nowhere else.** That list
# is the single source of truth for which files these checks apply to; the driver
# appends the Checks below to the project-wide set for files matching it. Adding a
# realtime subsystem means adding one entry there.
#
# clang-tidy's native mechanism for this is a .clang-tidy file inside each
# realtime directory, which Phase 0 could not use because none of those
# directories existed yet.
#
# How the two halves of the ban work:
#
#   types      banned by banning the header they live in
#              (portability-restrict-system-includes) - std::vector, std::string,
#              std::mutex, std::lock_guard, std::shared_ptr, std::function,
#              std::cout and the rest are unreachable without their header, and
#              this also catches them transitively through any engine header a
#              realtime file includes.
#   functions  banned by name (bugprone-unsafe-functions.CustomFunctions) -
#              printf and friends, abort, exit, rand, and the sleeps.
#   new/delete cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory plus the <new> header ban.
#   malloc     cppcoreguidelines-no-malloc.
#   throw      bugprone-exception-escape, against the noexcept that every function
#              reachable from process() carries (phase_0.md §4.2).
#   unbounded  misc-no-recursion - recursion has no bound the audio thread can
#              rely on.
#
# Check options live in the root .clang-tidy so there is one place to look for
# check configuration; they are inert wherever the check itself is off.
Checks: >
  bugprone-exception-escape,
  bugprone-unsafe-functions,
  cppcoreguidelines-no-malloc,
  cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory,
  misc-no-recursion,
  portability-restrict-system-includes
...
